🔹 Basic Linux Commands:
✅ mkdir → To create directories (folders)
✅ ls -la → List files & directories in specific path (even hidden ones)
✅ cd → Change directory (move between directories)
✅ pwd → Display current directory

🔹 File Operations:
✅ touch → To create an empty file
✅ cp → Copy files & directories
✅ mv → Move or rename files
✅ rm → Remove files or directories

🔹 Viewing and Editing Files:
✅ cat → View file content
✅ head → Display the beginning of the file
✅ tail → Display the end of the file

🔹 System Information:
✅ uname → Display OS info
✅ top/htop → Monitor live CPU & memory stats
✅ uptime → Show system uptime

🔹 File Permissions:
✅ chmod → Change file permissions
✅ chown → Change owner of a file
✅ umask → Set default permissions for new files

🔹 Networking Commands:
✅ ping → Check network connectivity
✅ netstat → Display network connections
✅ telnet → Check if ports are open

🔹 Process Management:
✅ ps → View running processes
✅ kill → Terminate running processes

🔹 Searching Files:
✅ grep → Search for patterns in files
✅ find → Locate files
✅ awk → Process and manipulate text

🔹 User Management:
✅ whoami → Show current user
✅ who → List logged-in users
✅ adduser → Add a user
✅ passwd → Change user password

🔹 Disk & Storage Management:
✅ df -h → Check disk space
✅ du -sh foldername → Check directory size
